<article class="template template-article" data-layout="blog-article" hidden>
  <header>
    <h2>Why quiet interfaces leave room for thought</h2>
    <p class="article-meta">Mara Voss, August 12, 2026, 6 minute read</p>
  </header>
  <div class="article-body">
    <p>
      Good interfaces do not compete with the work. They give each choice enough
      space, make the next action clear, and keep decoration in a supporting
      role.
    </p>
    <p>
      Typography carries much of that calm. A confident heading creates
      direction. A steady body face lets the reader settle into longer ideas
      without effort.
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Restraint is not an empty room. It is a room where every object has a
      reason to stay.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The best pairings feel distinct at first glance and coherent after several
      paragraphs. Contrast creates hierarchy, while shared proportions keep the
      page together.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
